+/*
+ * THE TWO TLS PROPERTIES OF A STREAM, which an application reads to look at the connection it is
+ * about to trust. MoneyMoney reads both: it talks to banks, and checking the certificate chain is
+ * the whole point of it.
+ *
+ * They are STRINGS and referencing them is a link edit: without them dyld refuses to load the
+ * process at all, before any window exists. That is where MoneyMoney stopped.
+ *
+ * The names are the documented ones, so a stream implementation that grows these properties later
+ * will answer to the same keys.
+ */
+const CFStringRef kCFStreamPropertySSLContext = CFSTR("kCFStreamPropertySSLContext");
+const CFStringRef kCFStreamPropertySSLPeerTrust = CFSTR("kCFStreamPropertySSLPeerTrust");
